// Fixture: ζ — a RepresentationWithin subject that declares NO realization.
// Task ζ (6169), cli_representation_within.rs, PRD C-SURFACE 1.
//
// The complement of the sibling representation_within_build_surface.ri. Both
// reach `reify check` with an EMPTY achieved_repr_tol, but for OPPOSITE
// reasons — and the remedy the user is given must differ accordingly:
//
//   sibling (a sphere at #precision(0.3mm))
//     OCCT build : tessellation measures it  → map non-empty → Satisfied
//     stub build : no kernel to measure with → map empty     → "build with OCCT"
//
//   here (no geometry at all)
//     OCCT build : a kernel IS live, but there is nothing to tessellate for
//                  this subject                → map empty
//     stub build : no kernel either            → map empty
//
// On an OCCT-enabled binary this fixture is the shape that made the pre-fix
// remedy a FALSE statement: it told the user to "build with OCCT" while OCCT
// was demonstrably live (the sibling fixture reports OK on the very same
// binary), which is a dead end and the same INV-SF-4 misattribution ζ exists
// to remove — merely relocated from the operand kinds to the kernel.
//
// So MyGeom deliberately has NO realization: the absence is the entire point
// of the fixture, and giving it any geometry would destroy what it gates.
//
// `param subject : MyGeom = MyGeom()` carries a DEFAULT for the same reason as
// in the sibling: only a *defined* StructureInstance operand reaches the
// language-level checker's misattributed "operator undefined for these operand
// kinds" branch, so the default is what lets this fixture independently re-pin
// C-SURFACE (1) on a second shape.
//
// Under `reify check` + OCCT: a kernel is registered but nothing was
// tessellated for the subject → Indeterminate (C1), explained by a
// cause-NEUTRAL Info that names neither the kernel nor OCCT → exit 0.
// Indeterminate is not a failure.
//
// Under `reify check` + stub (no OCCT): the map is empty because there is no
// kernel at all, so that surface legitimately DOES name the kernel. The CLI
// gate is OCCT-gated for exactly that reason — asserting the negative in stub
// mode would be wrong.
//
// Declares its module explicitly: without it, `reify check` also emits
// W_MODULE_DECL_MISSING (spec §7.1), and a committed fixture should not carry
// an avoidable warning.

module representation_within_no_realization

// MyGeom: a named structure type for `subject` to refer to. It carries only a
// scalar param — no `sphere(..)`, no `let` binding a solid, hence no
// realization for tessellation to measure.
structure MyGeom {
    param x : Real = 1.0
}

// Checker: declares the RepresentationWithin assertion over a subject that
// cannot be measured on any surface, because it has nothing to measure.
structure Checker {
    param subject : MyGeom = MyGeom()
    constraint RepresentationWithin(subject, 1mm)
}
